      "routePreference": "preferred",
      "explanationAfterStep": "The tin radical abstracts the iodine atom. A strong Sn–I bond forms and a weak C–I bond breaks, so the step is fast and downhill. The carbon radical is flat: the stereocentre that carried iodine is lost, which does not matter because that carbon becomes a CH₂."
    },
    {
      "stepKey": "hydrogen-transfer",
      "stepKind": "radical",
      "toStateId": "products",
      "fromStateId": "carbon-radical",
      "canonicalArrows": [
        "rad C7 ~> σ C7-H41",
        "σ Sn40-H41 ~> σ C7-H41",
        "σ Sn40-H41 ~> rad Sn40"
      ],
      "routePreference": "preferred",
      "explanationAfterStep": "The carbon radical takes a hydrogen atom from Bu₃SnH. The new Bu₃Sn• abstracts iodine from the next iodolactone: a chain. Overall the C–I bond has become C–H."
    }
  ],
